  "diagrams": [
    {
      "slug": "gate",
      "kind": "pipeline",
      "why": "The check is three ordered steps of one command, and each one fails the build on its own, so a pipeline is its real shape.",
      "label": "How go-lint runs. Your repository's check command calls vlint, pinned in mise.toml, in three steps. First vlint golangci -check builds .golangci.yml from the shared config plus your overlay and fails when the committed file drifts. Then vlint ./... runs the seven analyzers: layout, clockseam, envroot, errstring, noskipenv, doccomment and adrref. Last, golangci-lint runs with the generated config. Any step that finds something fails the check.",
      "gap": 96,
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "1 config",
          "sub": "vlint golangci -check",
          "rows": [
            "shared.yml",
            "+ your overlay",
            ".golangci.yml",
